  "Question": "The temperature varies according to \\(y=10+8\\sin(\\omega t)\\). What is the lowest temperature?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Assume, as in the recorded qualification, that \\(\\omega\\ne0\\) and the time domain contains a point where \\(\\sin(\\omega t)=-1\\). The minimum value of sine is \\(-1\\), so the lowest temperature is \\(10+8\\times(-1)=10-8=2\\).\n\nThe time-domain condition matters. For example, if \\(\\omega=1\\) and \\(0\\le t\\le\\pi\\), then \\(\\sin t\\ge0\\), with equality at the endpoints, so the lowest temperature is \\(10\\). If the nonconstant assumption is also dropped, \\(\\omega=0\\) gives the constant temperature \\(10\\).\n\nThus \\(2\\) is the intended answer under the recorded assumptions; without them, the lowest temperature is not uniquely determined.",
